# Lab: Username enumeration via subtly different responses

## Objective

Enumerate a valid username by identifying a subtle difference in the login response, brute-force the user's password, and access their account page.

## Solution

Step 1: Open the lab login page and submit an invalid username and password.

        Username: test
        Password: test

Step 2: Capture the login request in Burp Suite.

        Burp Suite → Proxy → HTTP history

Step 3: Send the login request to Intruder.

        Right-click the POST /login request
        → Send to Intruder

Step 4: Set the username as the payload position.

        username=§test§&password=test

Step 5: Go to the Payloads tab.

        Payload type: Simple list

        Paste the candidate usernames provided by PortSwigger.

Step 6: Configure Grep - Extract.

        Intruder → Settings → Grep - Extract → Add

        Find the following response:

        <p class=is-warning>Invalid username or password.</p>

        Select only:

        Invalid username or password.

        Click OK.

Step 7: Start the Intruder attack.

        Look at the Grep - Extract column.

        Most usernames will return:

        Invalid username or password.

        One username will have a subtly different response.

        The difference is a trailing space instead of the normal
        full stop formatting.

Step 8: Identify and record the username with the different response.

        If the difference is difficult to see:
        - Sort the Grep - Extract column.
        - Open the unusual response.
        - Use Burp Comparer to compare it with a normal response.

Step 9: Change the Intruder payload position from username to password.

        username=VALID_USERNAME&password=§invalid-password§

Step 10: Go to the Payloads tab.

        Payload type: Simple list

        Paste the candidate passwords provided by PortSwigger.

Step 11: Start the password attack.

        Check the Status code and response length.

        Incorrect passwords normally return:

        200

        The correct password returns:

        302

Step 12: Record the correct password.

        Password: daniel

Step 13: Return to the login page and log in using the discovered
username and password.

        Username: VALID_USERNAME
        Password: daniel

Step 14: Access the user's account page.

        The lab should now be marked as solved.

Congratulations!! you have solved this problem!!
